<title>GERMANY: German millers raised 1995/96 wheat, rye volumes.</title>
<headline>German millers raised 1995/96 wheat, rye volumes.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's milling industry processed 6.91 million tonnes of grain for breadmaking in 1995/96 (July/June), up from 6.88 million in the previous season, official farm ministry data showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Soft wheat accounted for 5.87 million tonnes (5.85 million in 1994/95) and rye for 1.04 million (1.03 million).</p>
<p>Milling for export rose to 605,000 tonnes from 586,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
